{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.fullEnergy_b3_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.fullEnergy_b3_neg","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L163-L169","doc":"**And it is negative for every substrate modulus.** The wrong sign is structural, not a\nnumerical accident at `q₀`: no `q > 0` makes this reading reproduce a positive `b₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.fullEnergy_b3_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.fullEnergy_b3_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L155-L161","doc":"**The full-energy reading gives `b₃ = −3(q + q⁻¹)` on the canonical carriers** — an exact closed\nform, with the Hopf clasp at `(2,0)` and the Borromean carrier at `(3,3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.fullPairEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.fullPairEnergy","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L150-L153","doc":"The full inter-component mutual energy of a crossing pair, `n₊·q − n₋·q⁻¹`\n(`QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel.pairEnergy`, restated here to keep this file's import cone\nsmall). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.offLocus_b3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.offLocus_b3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L121-L130","doc":"**Non-vacuity: the channel is not obstructed.** A carrier pair off the degenerate locus does\ngive a nonzero cumulant — here `μ_pair = 7`, `μ_triple = 51/2`, which lands `b₃/b₂` within 0.27 % of\nthe measured value. So the failure above is the carrier assignment, not the channel. Two free\ncrossing integers against one measured ratio is a fit, which is why this is recorded as a\npossibility rather than a result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.carrier_must_break_three_to_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.carrier_must_break_three_to_one","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L114-L119","doc":"**The criterion a replacement carrier must meet.** Any carrier pair reproducing a nonzero `b₃`\nin this channel must break the three-to-one multiplicity relation. Stated as the contrapositive of\n`b3_eq_zero_iff`, it is the one-line test to run against a proposed carrier before anything else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.canonical_carriers_ratio_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.canonical_carriers_ratio_zero","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L107-L112","doc":"**And the miss is total, not partial**: the predicted cumulant ratio is `0`, so the model\nsupplies none of the measured `b₃/b₂ = 0.6411239316`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.canonical_carriers_b3_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.canonical_carriers_b3_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L99-L105","doc":"**The canonical carriers sit on the degenerate locus.** `μ_Borromean = 3 = 3 · μ_Hopf`, so the\ncount channel predicts `b₃ = 0` for the framework's own `A = 2` and `A = 3` carriers — against a\nmeasured `b₃ = +1.4262225`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.borromeanMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.borromeanMult","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L96-L97","doc":"The Borromean carrier `L6a4` has `n₊ = n₋ = 3`, hence count multiplicity `½(3+3) = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.hopfMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.hopfMult","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L93-L94","doc":"The deuteron's Hopf clasp has `n₊ = 2`, `n₋ = 0`, hence count multiplicity `½(2+0) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.b3_over_b2_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.b3_over_b2_eq","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L86-L91","doc":"**The scale cancels.** The cumulant ratio depends only on the multiplicities, so no choice of\nthe MeV scale `s` or the substrate factor `h` can move it — this is a zero-parameter test. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.b3_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.b3_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L71-L84","doc":"**The cumulant vanishes exactly on the pair-local locus.** With a nonzero scale and a nonzero\nsubstrate factor, `b₃ = 0` iff the triple's count multiplicity is three times the pair's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.b3OfMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.b3OfMult","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L67-L69","doc":"The connected 3-body cumulant assembled from count-channel carriers: the triple's binding less\nthree times the pair's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.countBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CountChannelCarrierLocus.countBinding","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CountChannelCarrierLocus.lean#L63-L65","doc":"A carrier's binding in the count channel: the MeV scale `s`, the count multiplicity\n`μ = ½(n₊+n₋)`, and the substrate factor `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}